# Changelog

All notable changes to the "DLUnire Dark" extension will be documented in this file.

## [1.0.7] — 2026-09-04

### Added

* Añadido soporte para el resaltado de **código en línea de Markdown (Inline Code)**, con un color específico para distinguirlo visualmente del texto convencional.

## [1.0.6] - 2026-09-03

### Changed

* Color de comentarios de línea (`comment`, `comment.line.double-slash`, etc.) cambiado de `#ffffff60` a `#6b7490`, reduciendo el contraste general para mitigar el choque visual con anotaciones resaltadas por extensiones externas (Todo Tree, Better Comments) sobre `TODO`/`FIXME`, dado que la gramática TextMate de PHP no distingue esas anotaciones con un scope propio.

### Added

* Color dedicado para comentarios de bloque y documentación (`comment.block.documentation`, `comment.block`) en `#456e7e`, separándolos semánticamente de los comentarios de línea.
* Soporte para las nuevas claves de tema `modernEditorTab.*` y `modernTab.*` (pestañas del editor y de la terminal).
* `editor.border` (`#00aaff50`).
* `editor.snippetTabstopHighlightBackground` (`#0091ff33`).

## [1.0.5] - 2026-08-29

### Added

* **DL Typed Environment Support:** Full, dedicated token colorization and grammar rules for the DL Typed Environment (`dlunire.type`, `dlunire.varname`, `dlunire.colon`, `dlunire.operator.assign`, `dlunire.value.numeric`, `dlunire.value.boolean`, `dlunire.value.email`, `dlunire.value.uuid`, and block/documentation comments).
* **Multi-Language Syntax Specialization:**
  * **Rust:** Lifetimes (`#fff700`), enum members (`#7bff42`), native structs (`#00ff00`), declaration traits/structs and borrow operators (`#FF4B00`), plus dedicated semantic tokens (`keyword:rust`, `keyword.unsafe:rust`, `keyword.constant:rust`, `selfKeyword:rust`).
  * **C / C++:** Preprocessor includes (`#ffffffa0`), directives (`#ffff00`), preprocessor functions (`#f4a0ff`), function calls (`#a090ff`), code blocks (`#ffffa0`), built-in primitives (`#00ff00`), and POSIX reserved types (`#ffff00`).
  * **C# (.NET):** Exhaustive primitive types (`keyword.type.*.cs` in `#00ff00`), identifiers/fields/properties/parameters (`#20c0ff`), namespaces (`#40dfff`), and semantic tokens for `method:csharp` (`#00ffff`) and `field:csharp` (`#ff7700`).
  * **CSS / SCSS / Svelte:** Properties (`#00ff00`), values/colors (`#ff5000`), pseudo-classes/elements (`#ffff00`), custom variables `--*` (`#ff6000`), at-rules/directives (`#ff0060`), and full Svelte template token support.
  * **HTML / XML:** Tags (`#00ffff`), attributes (`#ff20d0`), double-quoted strings (`#ffc000`), single-quoted strings (`#ff9000`), unquoted strings (`#ffff00`), and attribute assignment operators (`#ffa0ff`).
  * **Shell (Bash) & Windows Batch:** Commands, functions, expansion and positional parameters for Shell; Batch commands, variables, and expressions.
  * **SQL & YAML:** DML statements and YAML tags highlighted in `#00ff00`.
  * **PHP & Python:** Magic methods (`#fc3bff`), PHP parameter placeholders (`#a4e1ff`), constructor functions (`#ff8000`), method invocations (`#ffd900`), and output constructs (`echo`/`print` in `#ffbd00`).
  * **JSON:** Keys (`#00ff00`), string values (`#ffc000`), and language constants/booleans (`#f196ff`).
* **Universal Native Classes:** Added universal scope rule for native language classes (`support.class` in `#00ff00`).
* **Semantic Diagnostics:** Added `unresolvedReference` highlighted in crimson red (`#ff0050`) for immediate visual error feedback.
* **In-Depth Syntax Documentation:** Added comprehensive chromatic hierarchy and scope documentation directly inside `DLUnire Dark Cyber`.

### Changed

* **Unified Syntax Highlighting Architecture:** Overhauled and synchronized `tokenColors` and `semanticTokenColors` across all 4 theme variants (`DLUnire Dark`, `DLUnire Dark Soft`, `DLUnire Dark Cyber`, `DLUnire Dark Cyber Soft`), removing obsolete legacy token structures.
* **Universal Scopes & Semantics:** Mapped user-defined constants (`constant`, `constant.other`) to the identifier palette (`#20c0ff`).
* **Numbers & Numeric Literals:** Standardized numeric literals to pure yellow `#ffff00` across TextMate and DL Typed Environment.
* **Parameter Inlay Hints:** Tuned `editorInlayHint.parameterForeground` (`#00ffaaa0`) and `editorInlayHint.parameterBackground` (`#00ffaa08`) for optimal legibility without visual clutter.
* **UI & Terminal Polish:** Harmonized Git and GitLens decoration colors for added/untracked resources (`#00ff00`), and updated terminal ANSI green and bright green palette (`#00ff00`).
* **Build System & Tooling:** Migrated build and publishing workflows in `Makefile` to use **Bun** (`bun run package`, `bun run publish:*`).
* **Formatting & Sanitation:** Cleaned trailing commas and strict JSON formatting across all theme files.

### Removed

* **Asset Optimization:** Cleaned up redundant preview screenshots and video, consolidating preview assets into a single lightweight, high-resolution [`images/preview.webp`](./images/preview.webp).

## [1.0.4] - 2026-08-08

### Added

* **New Variant: "DLUnire Dark Cyber"** — a high-saturation cyberpunk take on the base palette, sharing the same ultra-dark `#010305` background but with a distinct accent system: cyan for variables, magenta for functions, green for classes, violet for interfaces, and amber for strings. Structs, enums, and interfaces each get their own color instead of collapsing into "Classes."
* **New Variant: "DLUnire Dark Cyber Soft"** — the Cyber palette on a softer, blue-teal-tinted dark background, for long sessions where the full-contrast Cyber background feels too intense.
* **Diagnostics coloring:** `editorError`/`editorWarning`/`editorInfo`/`editorHint` foreground and matching Problems panel icons, previously falling back to VS Code defaults in the Cyber variants.
* **Bracket pair colorization:** `editorBracketHighlight.*` tuned to the palette instead of using default colors.
* **Git decoration:** added missing `addedResourceForeground` and `renamedResourceForeground`.

### Fixed

* **Invalid syntax highlighting** was the same color as the editor foreground, making syntax errors effectively invisible in the Cyber variants. Now rendered in red with an underline.
* **String literals** shared their color with the default editor foreground, reducing readability. Strings now have their own amber tone.
* **Semantic differentiation:** `class`, `interface`, `struct`, and `enum` previously resolved to near-identical hues in Cyber. Each now has a distinct, consistent color.
* **Editor chrome border consistency:** Activity Bar, Title Bar, Sidebar, and Status Bar borders now follow a single coherent hue-and-opacity system per variant, instead of mismatched one-off values.

## [1.0.3] - 2026-08-07

### Changed

* **UI/UX Consistency & Polish:** Comprehensive visual overhaul of auxiliary IDE components to maintain strict alignment with the DLUnire ecosystem:
  * **Peek View:** Complete thematic redesign of definition and reference panels (`peekViewTitle`, `peekViewEditor`, `peekViewResult`) to eliminate default blue/gray elements.
  * **Git & GitLens:** Integrated native git decorations and GitLens inline blame annotations / status indicators directly into the ultra-dark palette.
  * **Editor Widgets & Menus:** Refined search/replace widgets, context menus, and command palettes for seamless aesthetic continuity.
* **Infrastructure:** Streamlined multi-platform release workflows using a dedicated `Makefile` for atomic builds and publishing.

## [1.0.2] - 2026-08-05

### Added

* **New Variant:** Introduced **"DLUnire Dark Soft"**, featuring a slightly elevated graphite/slate background (`#07090b`) designed to reduce visual fatigue during long coding sessions while preserving strict dark-mode principles.
